  "worked_solution": "The number $0$ is a root of $f(x)$ if $f(0)=0.$ Of the given tables, only the following table has this property:\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $4$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $-5$ | $-7$ |",
